17. Banker's Algorithm

Aim:
To implement the Banker's algorithm for deadlock avoidance.

Pseudocode:

START
    Read number of processes and resources
    Read allocation matrix
    Read maximum matrix
    Calculate Need matrix
    Calculate Available resources
    Find a process whose Need <= Available
    Add its allocated resources to Available
    Repeat until all processes finish
    IF all processes finish
        System is in safe state
    ELSE
        System is unsafe
    END IF
STOP

Result:
Thus, the Banker's algorithm was successfully implemented to determine the safe state of the system.

